<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The iOS app's entitlements (project.yml). Sign in with Apple (AppleSignInPlatform): the App ID com.edde746.tortuga has
the capability as a primary App ID, so the development and distribution profiles Xcode makes for team G88U5B5783 carry
it. Associated Domains: a title's link (https://usetortuga.app/t/…, which Detail's Share sends) opens the app as a
Universal Link, the site's /.well-known/apple-app-site-association naming this App ID; the App ID needs the
Associated Domains capability, which the profiles then carry. The tvOS app adds the Top Shelf's App Group
(Tortuga-tvOS.entitlements) and has no Universal Links (no browser); the macOS app signs with its own files
(../AppKit/Tortuga-macOS.entitlements, and the UI tests' for a development-signed run).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.applesignin</key>
	<array>
		<string>Default</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:usetortuga.app</string>
	</array>
</dict>
</plist>
